<div class="wrap">

  <header>
    <div class="eyebrow">Plan E · Phase 2 · SDD Plan</div>
    <h1>mxPortdb — the iss1 private-MIB pilot</h1>
    <p class="standfirst">
      Phase 1 already made every entry register locally and every GET forward through the
      children chain. mxPortdb is therefore <em>already running this path</em>. Phase 2 does not
      wire anything up — it proves the path is correct on one representative MIB, and produces
      the number Phase 4's go/no-go will be argued from.
    </p>

    <dl class="facts">
      <div class="fact"><dt>Entries</dt><dd>17 · RO 9 / RW 8</dd></div>
      <div class="fact"><dt>OID root</dt><dd>…8691.603.1.1</dd></div>
      <div class="fact"><dt>URIs</dt><dd>1 scalar + 4 tables</dd></div>
      <div class="fact"><dt>Expected code change</dt><dd>none</dd></div>
      <div class="fact"><dt>DUT</dt><dd>192.168.127.253</dd></div>
    </dl>
  </header>

  <section>
    <h2>Why this can start code-free</h2>
    <p class="section-note">
      Three facts, each read from source rather than assumed.
    </p>
    <div class="rules">
      <div class="rule-row">
        <div class="rule-key">ISS side</div>
        <div class="rule-val">
          <strong><code>RegisterMXPORT()</code> already exists</strong> —
          <code>mxPortwr.c:31</code>, called unconditionally from <code>isssys.c:2744</code>,
          with <code>PortConfigIndexGet()</code> in the same file. Nothing to add.
          Later phases <em>do</em> need ISS work: §9.1's mxLa / mxVlan / mxLldp have no wrapper.
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="rule-row">
        <div class="rule-key">master side</div>
        <div class="rule-val">
          All 17 entries are <code>iss_build = 1</code>, so they take the ISS generator and
          forward at the local/remote boundary introduced in <code>aa598f7</code>.
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="rule-row">
        <div class="rule-key">no synthesis</div>
        <div class="rule-val">
          Each of the four tables declares its own column 1, so
          <code>GenerateTableIndexEntry()</code> takes the <code>tableURI</code> branch and never
          reaches <code>CreateIndexEntry()</code>. That is the claim Task 1 must actually prove.
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>The gate chain</h2>
